// How bodies move over the ground (D32). Placeholder values, tuned by play.
//
// walk_speed_cm_per_s: walking speed on the reference terrain (cost 10),
//                      in centimetres per game second. 143 is a calm walk.
// terrain_costs:       cost of crossing one tile of each terrain, 10 being
//                      the reference; paths weigh tiles by it and bodies
//                      slow down by it (cost 15 = two thirds of the speed).
//                      None cannot be walked. Every terrain must appear.
// carry_capacity_g:    what a body can carry in all, in grams (D35).
//                      20 kg: thirteen branches, or fifty flints.
// speed_percent_at_full_load: walking speed at full load, in percent of
//                      the unloaded speed; linear in between.
// sight_tiles:         how far a body sees, in tiles on each axis, by the
//                      terrain where it stands when it sets off: the most
//                      open walkable tile among its own and the eight
//                      around it, so at a wood's edge it sees out (D32). A
//                      way round (a ford, a bridge, the end of a pond) is
//                      taken only within that square. Past it the body
//                      walks straight toward its target; an obstacle in
//                      sight whose end it does not see, it skirts (see
//                      skirt_budget_tiles), using only what it sees; when
//                      that leads nowhere it says so and the player finds
//                      the way: exploring and knowing the ways is the
//                      game. 60 m in the open,
//                      25 m in the heart of a wood. A body never
//                      stands on water or rock; their values apply only to
//                      a body put there by mistake. Every terrain must
//                      appear.
// path_budget_tiles:   tiles a path search may look at before it gives up
//                      and the body walks straight. 1500 finds the way
//                      round an obstacle up to thirty or forty tiles
//                      across in the open; the search then costs under
//                      half a millisecond however it ends.
// search_work_per_tick: tiles all the path searches of one tick may
//                      expand in all (forty searches at their whole
//                      budget). A search refused at once (a target out of
//                      sight) costs next to nothing, so a wave of
//                      thousands of orders clears in a few ticks. The
//                      rest wait for the next tick in their lane, in the
//                      order they came, looks again included; the search
//                      at the head of a lane runs even past what is left,
//                      the next tick repaying the excess: none waits for
//                      ever.
// player_share_percent: the part of that work kept for the bodies a
//                      player pilots; NPCs and animals have the rest. A
//                      lane that does not use its part leaves it to the
//                      other.
// skirt_budget_tiles:  tiles a body may expand in one look when an
//                      obstacle stops it and the way round is not in
//                      sight: it looks within what it sees for the point
//                      on the edge of its sight from which the target
//                      seems nearest by the way it would walk (beside the
//                      obstacle, or past its end), goes there and looks
//                      again. 15000 covers all a body sees in the open
//                      (121 x 121 tiles): a look then costs a few
//                      milliseconds at worst, within the work above.
// skirt_looks:         looks a body may take skirting obstacles for one
//                      order; then it gives up and says it is blocked. It
//                      gives up sooner when every point on the edge of
//                      its sight is ground it has already looked over for
//                      that order: it never circles at the bottom of a
//                      bay, nor walks back past where it has been.
(
    carry_capacity_g: 20000,
    speed_percent_at_full_load: 60,
    walk_speed_cm_per_s: 143,
    sight_tiles: {
        grass: 60,
        forest: 25,
        ford: 60,
        brook: 60,
        water: 60,
        rock: 60,
    },
    path_budget_tiles: 1500,
    search_work_per_tick: 60000,
    player_share_percent: 50,
    skirt_budget_tiles: 15000,
    skirt_looks: 24,
    terrain_costs: {
        grass: Some(10),
        forest: Some(15),
        ford: Some(20),
        brook: Some(15),
        water: None,
        rock: None,
    },
)
